{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact clean pushed head 5aab3697b714f966e25cb4596e12afea13b8e04d, against governing child 43ce23b0 and all ten exact-path artifacts.\n\nThe fix itself is right, and I want that on the record before the blocker. The seat copy is now truthful on every surface I could reach: an open game renders Black as Open, a secret-restricted and an invite-restricted game each render Black as Restricted, the game page and the lobby card now agree for the same game, occupied seats still render fingerprints with no admission wording, and the wording derives from AdmissionOpen, a boolean computed from the presence or absence of an invitation and nothing derived from the secret. The confidentiality argument is structural rather than conventional: Game.invitation is unexported, so encoding/json cannot marshal it and html/template cannot traverse it. Eight served artifacts plus the MCP surface were scanned with positive controls and none carried the secret, its digest, the invited fingerprint, or the private field names. The diff is exactly two files and seventeen lines: the seat block and assertions. All four gates are green, including -race.\n\nTHE BLOCKER: THE GUARD COVERS ONE OF THE TWO SEATS IT CHANGED.\n\ngame.html now carries two structurally identical seat lines, one for White and one for Black, each with the same three-way rule. Every assertion in the new test is written against the literal string \u003cdt\u003eBlack\u003c/dt\u003e, and every game in the fixture is created with --color white, so Black is always the empty seat. I confirmed both facts in the source at this head rather than inferring them.\n\nThe consequence was demonstrated, not argued. Reverting only the White line to the pre-fix unconditional Open leaves the entire suite green — ok on both packages, full run. The exact defect this commit exists to prevent can be reintroduced on the symmetric branch with no test noise at all. The same mutation on lobby.html:32's White branch also escapes.\n\nThat is the condition I wrote in 43ce23b0, and it is unmet as written: the test is required to be demonstrated to fail when the template regresses. The template did regress, on a line this commit authored, and the test did not fail.\n\nI want to be precise about severity, because it would be easy to overstate this. Shipped behaviour at this head is correct — a game created with --color black renders White as Restricted or Open truthfully, verified live against the running server. Nothing is broken for a user today. This is a coverage defect, and it is the kind that matters most in exactly this commit, because a truthfulness guard that only guards half of what it changed is the thing that lets the defect come back quietly. The whole point of the change was to stop a surface lying about admission; the test needs to be able to notice when it starts again.\n\nTHE REMEDY IS SMALL. In cmd/chess/main_test.go, add two games to the fixture created with --color black — one open and one restricted — and assert \u003cdt\u003eWhite\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003eRestricted\u003c/dd\u003e and \u003cdt\u003eWhite\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003eOpen\u003c/dd\u003e on their game pages, plus White restricted and White open on their lobby cards. Those are the strings the code already produces; I checked. Then break the White line alone and watch it fail, which is the check that was missing the first time. No production change is needed.\n\nTake the lobby with it. lobby.html:32 has the same half-width gap and it is pre-existing, arriving with the already-approved ba0e06bc rather than with this commit, so I am not counting it against this head. But it has the same single-root remedy, the fixture you are adding covers both surfaces at once, and leaving it would mean coming back to this file a third time. This class has already appeared three times in this lane and I would rather it ended here.\n\nARCHITECTURE: preserved, and there is still no architecture reference page in this repository — twenty tracked files and no docs tree, so there is nothing to check against and nothing to update. I state that explicitly rather than letting the conclusion pass by default. The fold is untouched. AdmissionOpen was already computed, already exported and already published as admission_open; the commit only consumes it in a template that already received the same value. No new field, no new data crossing the fold-to-view seam, no new HTTP surface.\n\nSECURITY: no unresolved defect, and no new boundary is crossed. The template gained read access to one boolean it could already read. Authorization is untouched: the secret comparison still uses a constant-time compare. The new wording discloses only that a game carries some restriction, which admission_open already published, and it does not distinguish a secret-restricted game from an invited one. Auto-escaping is in force.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION: nothing to cut; the change is a single else-if on an existing predicate, with no helper and no duplicated logic. One observation rather than a request: the three-way rule now exists in four near-identical copies across the two templates, and that duplication is exactly what let the White-seat mutations escape. I would still not abstract it — a shared partial would be more machinery for less clarity — which is precisely why the fixture should cover both seats instead.\n\nWHAT IS FRESH HERE AND WHAT IS CARRIED FORWARD, so this verdict is not mistaken for more than it is. Fresh this pass: everything above about the seat copy, the leak scan, the fourth-surface search, and the six mutations. Carried forward from my earlier verdict c603aa6b on ba0e06bc and NOT re-derived: the orphan-game reproduction and its disappearance, the twelve mutations from that pass, and the cross-version refusal checked by building binaries at two heads and crossing them. I did confirm this pass that CreateNamed still ends in a single append with all validation before it, that the binding is still chess-fold@2 with all four cross-version subtests passing, and that the promotion refusal still names the required piece in a real game played to a promotion.\n\nA METHOD NOTE I AM RECORDING AGAINST MYSELF. The first run of the leak scan reported every pattern clean, including controls that must hit, because the file list was passed unquoted and the shell handed grep one bogus path while the error was discarded. A scan that cannot fail is worth nothing. The result reported above is the corrected run, with positive controls that do hit. I mention it because the same shape has bitten this project before, and because a leak scan is exactly the check most likely to be believed without examination.\n\nNOT VERIFIED: no page was rendered in a real browser, so layout, CSS and app.js runtime behaviour are unchecked; every HTML conclusion comes from bytes served over HTTP. The lobby's game-state chip renders the lifecycle word open beside the admission copy for an unseated restricted game; it is truthful in its own vocabulary and out of scope here, but the word collision sits two spans from the admission wording and may be worth its own row.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:1b96687964cbba5a6089c526d7136b32ba9488a5#git:sha1:76591d9a4663b467d3f61da8ced83787823f097b","head":"5aab3697b714f966e25cb4596e12afea13b8e04d","verdict":"changes-requested"}}